diff --git a/docs/skate-multiplayer.md b/docs/skate-multiplayer.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..aa77b689
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/skate-multiplayer.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Multiplayer free skating
+
+The companion server is [vmangos-world-of-skatecraft](https://github.com/shaarmander/vmangos-world-of-skatecraft).
+Its SKATECRAFT.md defines protocol v1. Both sides must include this extension.
+
+Start the modified VMaNGOS world service and set `WOW_SKATE_MULTIPLAYER=1` before
+launching the client. Each client needs its own account; sharing one disconnects
+the previous session. Each player still presses J and uses their own controller.
+The custom clients display each other's full solved skeleton and separately
+animated deck, trucks and wheels. The server continues to run ordinary WoW.
+
+`skate/network.rs` publishes at 20 Hz, waits for the server handshake, buffers
+remote poses and samples 100 ms behind arrival. `rig.rs` retains a retargeting
+plan per entity; `board.rs` owns a separate skinned board for each remote entity.
+The ordinary network object remains the source of appearance and identity.
+
+This implementation trusts clients to simulate their skating. Scores, trick
+verification, shared board collisions and server-authoritative physics are outside
+this protocol. Unmodified servers should be used with the opt-in variable unset.
+
+For automated, noncombat testing only, `WOW_UNATTENDED=1 WOW_SKATE_PROBE=1`
+feeds a repeating push/crouch/ollie input sequence through the real Skate engine.
+`WOW_SKATE_AUTOSTART=5` starts riding after world entry. Use distinct probe accounts,
+separate `BENILLA_HOME` paths, `WOW_NOSOUND=1`, bounded run duration, and live
+screenshots to check appearance. Test receiving in both directions, then dismount,
+logout/reconnect and approach/departure from visibility range. Receiving packets
+alone does not establish that both the character rig and board are displayed.
+
+The Windows launcher `test-two-clients.bat` starts two locally provisioned test
+accounts with independent settings. `tools/test-skate-multiplayer.ps1 -Probe`
+runs a bounded capture and dismount/remount sequence; add `-Idle` to omit scripted
+pushes. Its local identity JSON is excluded from version control.
+
+Facing changes and normal movement are coalesced to 20 Hz while skating. This is
+necessary because physics heading jitter can otherwise flood the server with a
+SET_FACING packet on every rendered frame. Forced speed acknowledgments are still
+serviced immediately.
